ame_versions":32651,"id":32652,"slug":32653,"project_type":46,"team":32654,"organization":3589,"title":32655,"description":32656,"body":32657,"body_url":3589,"published":32658,"updated":32659,"approved":32660,"queued":32661,"status":29957,"requested_status":29957,"moderator_message":3589,"license":32662,"downloads":32663,"followers":30001,"categories":32664,"additional_categories":32665,"loaders":32666,"versions":32667,"icon_url":32669,"issues_url":3589,"source_url":3589,"wiki_url":3589,"discord_url":3589,"donation_urls":32670,"gallery":32671,"color":32676,"thread_id":32677,"monetization_status":30057},[709],"yPVMbdwm","realite","ZNhYKQPA","REAlite","Lightweight realistic shader with improved lighting, water, and sky effects for low end PCs","Realite Shader is a lightweight and realistic Minecraft shader designed to improve lighting, atmosphere, and visual quality while maintaining good performance.\n\n-  Sky with dynamic day-night cycle\n-  Sun and moon lighting with smooth transitions\n-  Reflective and wavy water with improved transparency\n-  Flat animated water waves\n-  Enhanced terrain lighting and shadows\n-  Improved sunset and sunrise visuals\n-  Balanced brightness,bright days and dark night\n\n\n\nThis shader is optimized for low-end systems and works well on integrated graphics\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Install Iris for 1.21.5\n2. Download the REAlite Shader Pack.\n3. Run iris in minecraft \n   launcher \n4. Under options, open video settings,then Shader Packs and install the REAlite shader \n5. Under Shader choose REAlite shader, make sure shaders are enabled\n\n## Why use Realite?\n\nRealite Shader focuses on delivering a cinematic and immersive experience without heavy performance loss, making it ideal for players who want better visuals on weaker hardware.","2026-04-03T06:44:24.447240Z","2026-04-10T08:37:27.107812Z","2026-04-08T06:38:32.841373Z","2026-04-04T12:03:28.017034Z",{"id":30072,"name":10,"url":3589},206,[],[],[362],[32668],"rJGgfmKa","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/yPVMbdwm/1f53cbbe84ab85650fdb90f69e3b354f9df8cb1e_96.webp",[],[32672],{"url":32673,"raw_url":32674,"featured":439,"title":3589,"description":3589,"created":32675,"ordering":30001},"https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/yPVMbdwm/images/5cfa09c4d3cfe5171254dc5a006150d44fd16a4b_350.webp","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/yPVMbdwm/images/5cfa09c4d3cfe5171254dc5a006150d44fd16a4b.png","2026-04-03T06:53:38.918206Z",16448250,"QQ8vvGId",{"client_side":29969,"server_side":30059,"game_versions":32679,"id":32680,"slug":32681,"project_type":31,"team":32682,"organization":3589,"title":32683,"description":32684,"body":32685,"body_url":3589,"published":32686,"updated":32687,"approved":32688,"queued":32689,"status":29957,"requested_status":29957,"moderator_message":3589,"license":32690,"downloads":30857,"followers":30001,"categories":32691,"additional_categories":32692,"loaders":32693,"versions":32694,"icon_url":32709,"issues_url":32710,"source_url":32711,"wiki_url":32712,"discord_url":32713,"donation_urls":32714,"gallery":32715,"color":32722,"thread_id":32723,"monetization_status":30057},[667,658,652,607,601,556,502,496,483],"yP7IdsBH","crowbar","APM71jVA","CrowBar","Adds skins and nametags to the player locator bar","[![CrowBar](https://castled.codes/assets/crowbar-banner.png)](https://github.com/castledking/CrowBar)\n\n\u003Cp align=\"center\">\n  \u003Ca href=\"https://discord.com/invite/pCKdCX6nYr\">\u003Cimg alt=\"Discord\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Discord-Community-5865F2?style=for-the-badge&logo=discord&logoColor=white\">\u003C/a>\n  \u003Ca href=\"https://github.com/castledking/CrowBar/issues\">\u003Cimg alt=\"GitHub Issues\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/GitHub-Issues-181717?style=for-the-badge&logo=github\">\u003C/a>\n  \u003Ca href=\"https://github.com/castledking/CrowBar/wiki\">\u003Cimg alt=\"Wiki\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/GitHub-Wiki-181717?style=for-the-badge&logo=github\">\u003C/a>\n  \u003Ca href=\"https://castled.codes\">\u003Cimg alt=\"CASTLED CODEX\" src=\"https://castled.codes/assets/logo-banner.png\" width=\"140\" height=\"35\">\u003C/a>\n\u003C/p>\n\nCrowBar is a Fabric client mod for Minecraft 1.21.6-1.21.11 and 26.1.x that extends the locator bar with readable player name tags, skin markers, distance text, team-colored dots, and a self-view capture mode.\n\n## Features\n\n- Renders player names above locator bar markers.\n- Can replace locator dots with player skin faces.\n- Shows optional distance text next to player names.\n- Preserves team colors when a team color is available.\n- Adds a self-view mode for clean locator bar screenshots.\n- Hides hearts, hunger, armor, and the vanilla locator bar while self-view mode is active.\n- Works as a client-side mod; servers do not need to install CrowBar.\n- Includes Mod Menu support for toggling features in-game.\n\n## Allium Servers\n\nAllium Essentials is an optional Paper server plugin that can send CrowBar a dedicated locator payload. When Allium is installed, CrowBar does not have to rely on vanilla locator waypoints: the server can send the player UUID, position, team color, and visibility state needed for the custom locator bar.\n\nThat lets CrowBar keep rendering players who are hidden, sneaking, invisible, or otherwise missing from vanilla waypoint data. It also lets the server keep NPC waypoint transmit range at zero while still giving CrowBar the real player data it needs.\n\nWithout Allium, CrowBar falls back to normal client-visible players, including LAN and integrated-server sessions.\n\n\u003Cp>\n  \u003Ca href=\"https://modrinth.com/plugin/allium-essentials#download\">\u003Cimg alt=\"Download Allium on Modrinth\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Download%20Allium-Modrinth-00AF5C?style=for-the-badge&logo=modrinth&logoColor=white\">\u003C/a>\n\u003C/p>\n\n## Requirements\n\nUse the jar that matches your Minecraft line:\n\n- `CrowBar-1.21.x`: Minecraft 1.21.6-1.21.11, Java 21, Fabric Loader 0.18.4 or newer, Fabric API 0.141.4 or newer.\n- `CrowBar-26.1.x`: Minecraft 26.1.x, Java 25, Fabric Loader 0.19.2 or newer, Fabric API 0.150.0 or newer.\n\nMod Menu is optional, but recommended for the config screen.\n\n## Controls\n\nDefault keybinds:\n\n- `N`: Toggle locator name tags\n- `B`: Toggle locator skins\n- `Z`: View self locator bar\n- `X`: Show distance\n\nKeybinds can be changed from Minecraft's controls menu under the CrowBar category.\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Install Fabric Loader for your Minecraft version.\n2. Install Fabric API.\n3. Put the matching CrowBar jar into your `mods` folder.\n4. Launch the game.\n\n## Building\n\n```bash\n./gradlew :version21:build :version26:build\n```\n\nThe built jars are written to `version21/build/libs/` and `version26/build/libs/`.\n\n## Links\n\n- Website: https://castled.codes\n- Issues: https://github.com/castledking/CrowBar/issues\n- Upstream inspiration: https://github.com/MCRcortex/headlocatorbar\n","2026-05-25T23:27:09.118111Z","2026-06-08T02:40:30.896894Z","2026-05-29T05:41:14.484167Z","2026-05-25T23:42:28.776613Z",{"id":31163,"name":31164,"url":3589},[175,275,303],[100,134,297],[346],[32695,32696,32697,32698,32699,32700,32701,32702,32703,32704,32705,32706,32707,32708],"y3EVs1Pl","LKSpi1hT","64iN9Zgm","PIUpADrG","5AMZG1gh","GgonTFAS","V5HYBRLK","JKp64JNc","P3dppoNG","63FlFbGw","P1dZAs1k","2tXqQhR7","ro0IkdHR","um0EpYTF","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/yP7IdsBH/6545fb2754da1314899e684a57079cdda483f349_96.webp","https://github.com/castledking/CrowBar/issues","https://github.com/castledking/CrowBar","https://github.com/castledking/CrowBar/wiki","https://discord.com/invite/pCKdCX6nYr",[],[32716],{"url":32717,"raw_url":32718,"featured":846,"title":32719,"description":32720,"created":32721,"ordering":29985},"https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/yP7IdsBH/images/41361be5a61469f03571b058fbce30b2fe7c4701_350.webp","https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/yP7IdsBH/images/41361be5a61469f03571b058fbce30b2fe7c4701.png","Skins and Nametags enabled","You can toggle 